Optimized Approach: With calculating the prefixSum i.e. if prefixSum-k is present over the HashMap
Core Logic : The core idea relies on a simple mathematical property of prefix sums.
Prefix Sum (Prefix_{i}): 
This is the cumulative sum of all elements from index 0 to index i.

Subarray Sum (k): If a subarray ending at index i sums up to (k), 
it means some earlier prefix sum (Prefix_{j}) must satisfy the equation: ( Prefix_{i}- Prefix_{j} = k)
Rearranging this gives: ( Prefix_{j}= Prefix_{i} -k )

The Hash Map: Your map stores <PrefixSum, First_Seen_Index>. 
By searching the map for rem = prefixSum - k, you are instantly checking if a matching earlier prefix sum exists. If it does, the subarray between those two indices sums to (k).
Time Complexity : O(N)

Solution:
class Solution {
    public int longestSubarray(int[] nums, int k) {
       int n=nums.length;
       int maxLen=0;
       HashMap<Integer,Integer> store=new HashMap<>();
       int prefixSum=0;
     //For handling prefiSum becoming zero initialize HashMap with (0,-1)
      store.put(0,-1);

       for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        prefixSum+=nums[i];
        store.put(prefixSum,i);

        if(prefixSum==k){
            maxLen=Math.max(maxLen,i+1);
        }

        int rem=prefixSum-k;
        if(store.containsKey(rem)){
            int len=i-store.get(rem);
            maxLen=Math.max(maxLen,len);
        }
       } 
       return maxLen;
    }
}

Optimal Solution: Using Two pointer Approach

Solution:
public class Main{
    public static void main(String args[]){
        int arr[]={1,1,1,1,1,2,2};int m=5;
        System.out.println(LongestSubarray(arr, m));
    }
       public static int LongestSubarray(int[] nums, int k) {
       int n=nums.length;
       int left_pointer=0;
       int right_pointer=0;
       int prefixSum=0;
       int maxLen=0;

       while(right_pointer<n){
        prefixSum+=nums[right_pointer];

        //Invalid Condition if prefixSumis greater than k then we will trim and make it equal to chk
        if(prefixSum>k){
          prefixSum-=nums[left_pointer];
          left_pointer++;
        }

        //Valid Condition
        if(prefixSum==k){
          maxLen=Math.max(maxLen,right_pointer-left_pointer+1);
        }
        right_pointer++;
       }
       return maxLen;
    }
}



